Licensing for this directory
============================

The rest of this repository is MIT licensed (see ../LICENSE). This directory is
NOT, and cannot be.

`patches/jdk21-build.patch` and `patches/romraider-5eat.patch` are diffs against
RomRaider, which is licensed GPL-2.0. They quote RomRaider's own source in their
context lines, and the code they add becomes part of RomRaider when applied. They
are therefore a derivative work of a GPL-2.0 program, and they are distributed
under the **GNU General Public License version 2 or later**, the same terms as
RomRaider itself.

The same applies to any binary built from them, including the standalone package
published on the Releases page. Its `license.txt` is RomRaider's GPL-2.0 text.

    RomRaider - https://github.com/RomRaider/RomRaider
    Copyright the RomRaider contributors
    Licensed under the GNU General Public License v2.0 or later

This is not a formality. If you redistribute the built package, GPL-2.0 requires
you to make the corresponding source available. That is satisfied by the patches in
this directory together with the pinned upstream revision recorded in
`build-standalone.sh`, which is why the revision is pinned rather than tracking
master.

What is covered by which licence:

| Path | Licence |
|---|---|
| `patches/*.patch` | GPL-2.0-or-later (derivative of RomRaider) |
| the built application | GPL-2.0-or-later |
| `build-standalone.sh`, `README.md`, `log4j.properties` | MIT, as the rest of the repo |
| the bundled Java runtime | GPL-2.0 with Classpath Exception (Eclipse Temurin) |
| the ROM images shipped in the package | Subaru/FHI firmware, not mine, no rights claimed |

Full GPL-2.0 text: https://www.gnu.org/licenses/old-licenses/gpl-2.0.txt
